 Training vs Testing

This is very important.


Suppose we have:


1000 data samples

We might split:


800 → Training
200 → Testing

Training data

Used to learn the model.


Testing data

Used to evaluate how the trained model performs on unseen data.


Why?


Because we don't want:



"The model memorized the training data."



We want:



"The model learned patterns that generalize to new data."




15. What is Overfitting?

One of the most common ML interview questions.


Imagine a student memorizes every question from a previous exam.


They get:


Previous questions → 100%

But when the questions change:


New questions → 50%

That's similar to overfitting.


In ML:


Training performance → Very high
Testing performance  → Poor

The model has learned the training data too specifically.



16. Underfitting

The opposite.


The model is too simple to capture the underlying pattern.


Training → Poor
Testing  → Poor

So:


Underfitting
→ Model too simple

Good fit
→ Learns useful patterns

Overfitting
→ Model memorizes training patterns


17. How do we reduce overfitting?

Common techniques:




More training data


Regularization


Cross-validation


Feature selection


Data augmentation


Early stopping


Simplifying the model


Dropout for neural networks



