20. Loss Function

Another important concept.


The model makes a prediction:


Actual = 100
Predicted = 80

There is an error.


A loss function measures how bad the prediction is.





Gradient Descent

How does a model actually improve its parameters?


One common optimization technique is Gradient Descent.


Imagine you're standing on a mountain and want to reach the lowest point.


       ●
      /
     /
    ●
   /
  ●
 ↓
Minimum

The algorithm repeatedly adjusts parameters in the direction that reduces the loss.





